  "rationale": "**Judgment: the sources support `requirements.examples.evidence`.**\n\n**Implementation**\n- **Missing evidence.** `inspect_repository_with_progress` (src/evidence.rs) pairs each non-term definition with `evidence/<full-name>.json`. If an example has none, it reports `evidence/<name>.json: missing for example at <source>`.\n- **Same checks as requirements.** `validate_evidence_file` handles requirements and examples alike. It picks the text field from the definition kind (`example` or `requirement`). It rejects unexpected or missing fields, validates the determination, rationale and inputs, and checks dependencies.\n- **Changed example text.** The same function compares the stored `example` string with the current body and reports \"example text changed at …\" followed by `compact_diff`.\n- **True determination without a `{test}`.** `validate_references` reports `example X has a true determination but no {test} reference`. The check counts `{test}` references and `:test:` anchors, and it only fires when the evidence determination is boolean `true`. A `FIXME` determination is not flagged.\n- **Test covered by an input.** `validate_references` also requires every non-`cite` reference to a definition to fall inside some evidence input range. A cited test therefore has to be covered. Whole-file anchors must be fully contained in an input.\n- **Reviewer guidance.** `initial_prompt` (src/authoring/mod.rs) builds the prompt from the approved template in md/requirements/authoring.md. That template says an example needs test setup and assertions covering its scenario, and that \"a true judgment needs at least one {test} reference\". It never offers the requirement no-test justification for examples. `DefinitionKind::noun` supplies the \"example\" and \"requirement\" wording used in these messages.\n- **Marking.** The relevant functions all carry `{impl}` markers for this requirement. Their other behavior is accounted for by the other `{impl}` markers on the same functions, for example schema, coverage and orphans.\n\n**Tests**\n- `cited_example_with_a_test_and_matching_evidence_validates` (src/evidence.rs) builds an example with a `{test}` reference and matching evidence, and checks that it validates. It then checks each of these failures:\n  - emptied inputs give \"no input covers … src/main.rs:1\";\n  - a changed test source gives \"input text changed\";\n  - a changed requirements glob gives \"requirements glob matches changed\";\n  - outdated example text gives \"example text changed\" and a `- Outdated.` diff line;\n  - the wrong field name gives \"missing field \\\"example\\\"\" and \"unexpected field \\\"requirement\\\"\";\n  - a deleted evidence file gives \"missing for example\".\n- `example_errors_include_duplicates_invalid_bodies_and_missing_tests` checks that a true determination with no test gives \"has a true determination but no {test} reference\".\n- `fixme_examples_pass_without_test_references_but_true_examples_do_not` (tests/outcomes.rs) checks three cases. A `FIXME` example with no test passes. Changing it to `true` gives the \"no {test} reference\" error. Changing it to `false` gives \"determination is false\".\n- The `fixture` helper in tests/outcomes.rs also carries a `{test}` marker for this requirement.\n\nThese tests cover the missing file, changed text with its diff, the true-without-test error, input coverage, determination validation, and the FIXME/true/false outcomes. I found no unmarked implementation and no untested part of the obligations.",
